<!--
  1vivy personal crDroid 16.0 ROM - OnePlus SM8850 (infiniti, macan, macanc,
  fairlady). FEATURES-V4 LANE GOVERNED MANIFEST.

  Drop into .repo/local_manifests/ as 1vivy-features-v4.xml after:

      repo init -u https://github.com/crdroidandroid/android.git -b 16.0
      # base manifest pinned at a311bc97e4784ee24e8f97e377d06bdbff85b4bb

  then `repo sync`.

  USE THIS FILE INSTEAD OF 1vivy-rom.xml AND 1vivy-features-v2.xml - NEVER
  ALONGSIDE EITHER. All three declare the same paths, so placing two in
  local_manifests/ at once is a configuration error.

  THIS MANIFEST IS PUBLISHED-HEAD, exactly as features-v2 was. Every camera-port
  revision below is at or past the head the published patch profile would
  produce. DO NOT run patches/patch/apply-patches.py against a tree synced from
  this file: the profile is already contained in these heads by construction and
  replaying it would DOUBLE-APPLY. 1vivy-rom.xml is the opposite lane - it pins
  the profile BASE commits and the replay there is mandatory.

  Composed 2026-08-11, derived mechanically from 1vivy-features-v2.xml by
  swapping the eight 1vivy topic revisions from staging/features-v2/all-v2 to
  staging/features-v4/all. Nothing else changed, and that is a measured claim:
  the four camera-port SHA pins were re-read from the real remote this session
  with `git ls-remote` and every one is UNCHANGED since v2 was composed -

      android_frameworks_av              bade1ca9f81d7b819e27d39497349531359c3b9f
      android_frameworks_native          7e6caf56f2a6550e89e03286cbc9f3401629b2c3
      android_device_qcom_sepolicy_vndr  838178d538901e80223d2e638df45d7295ffeb48
      android_packages_apps_Sandbox      83d599f08df598770926afcccfd860f979418678

  so the composition inputs are already current and no pin refresh was owed.

  Eight topic-bearing repos ride staging/features-v4/all. Four of them carry new
  work landed from the features-v4 TAKE set; the other four carry the identical
  tree as staging/features-v2/all-v2 and exist so the generation is uniform and
  future v4 topics have a branch to land on. Which is which is recorded in
  .omo/evidence/features-v4/06-landing-receipt.md - a repo with no new commits
  is a measured outcome here, not an oversight.

  macan, macanc and fairlady stay on 16.0: they carry ZERO topic branches under
  staging/* or archive/*, proven by the same `git ls-remote` sweep that returned
  34 and 41 branches for infiniti and sm8850-common.

  Only lineage_infiniti-bp4a-userdebug is built and runtime-validated. macan,
  macanc and fairlady are present for source closure and static lunch
  resolution; no runtime result is implied for them.
-->
